--TEST--
PHP's `__construct` gets its own diagnostic naming `constructor`, rather than the generic camelCase one — `rule:classes/constructor-is-a-method-named-constructor`
--FILE--
<?nvs
class Old {
    public int $n = 0;

    public function __construct(int $n) {
        $this->n = $n;
    }
}
echo "unreachable\n";
// covers: lang:classes/declaring-a-class
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0114]: Novis's constructor is spelled `constructor`, not `__construct`
  --> case.nvs:5:21
